cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below, and cite the original NPDP Bench listed in references.
title: "NPDP Bench: non-serial polyadic dynamic programming benchmarks for polyhedral compilers"
abstract: >-
  Twelve non-serial polyadic dynamic programming (NPDP) kernels (RNA folding,
  sequence alignment, matrix chain multiplication, optimal binary search
  trees, polygon triangulation) written as static control parts with
  contiguous arrays, symbolic size parameters and no function calls, to
  evaluate automatic source-to-source optimizing compilers (Pluto, PPCG, ...)
  and manual transformations. Includes correctness tests, reference checksums
  and a benchmarking driver.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zetsyog/NPDP_Bench"
authors:
  - family-names: "Rossetti"
    given-names: "Clément"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3495-5641"
keywords:
  - polyhedral compilation
  - loop tiling
  - dynamic programming
  - NPDP
  - benchmark
  - OpenMP
references:
